From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UN1CA <unica@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 19 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] a52sxq: default AOD to fullscreen and always on

The native fullscreen capability is supplied through the target floating
feature configuration. These per-user system settings make AOD enabled and
continuously shown when SettingsProvider initializes a new user database.

---
 smali/com/android/providers/settings/DatabaseHelper$1.smali | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/smali/com/android/providers/settings/DatabaseHelper$1.smali b/smali/com/android/providers/settings/DatabaseHelper$1.smali
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/smali/com/android/providers/settings/DatabaseHelper$1.smali
+++ b/smali/com/android/providers/settings/DatabaseHelper$1.smali
@@ -437,1 +437,6 @@
     invoke-static {v0, v2, v8, v1}, Landroid/provider/Settings$System;->putIntForUser(Landroid/content/ContentResolver;Ljava/lang/String;II)Z
+    const/4 v2, 0x1
+    const-string v3, "aod_mode"
+    invoke-static {v0, v3, v2, v1}, Landroid/provider/Settings$System;->putIntForUser(Landroid/content/ContentResolver;Ljava/lang/String;II)Z
+    const-string v3, "aod_show_state"
+    invoke-static {v0, v3, v2, v1}, Landroid/provider/Settings$System;->putIntForUser(Landroid/content/ContentResolver;Ljava/lang/String;II)Z
--
2.51.0
